d3dcompiler_47.dll built from vkd3d
===================================

This d3dcompiler_47.dll is an open-source stand-in for Microsoft's HLSL
compiler DLL. It is libvkd3d-utils (the D3DCompile/D3DReflect family) and
libvkd3d-shader (the HLSL compiler) linked statically into one DLL with the
same export names as Windows' d3dcompiler_47.dll. It depends only on the C
runtime and kernel32, so it can be copied next to any program.

It is installed outside bin/ on purpose, so that it does not replace the
system DLL for every program on PATH:

    $MINGW_PREFIX/lib/vkd3d-d3dcompiler/d3dcompiler_47.dll

To use it for one program, copy it into that program's directory (Windows
loads DLLs from the executable's directory before System32):

    cp $MINGW_PREFIX/lib/vkd3d-d3dcompiler/d3dcompiler_47.dll /path/to/app/

For .NET tools (e.g. MonoGame's mgfxc via SharpDX.D3DCompiler) put it next
to the tool's .dll/.exe; for a tool started through `dotnet tool.dll` that is
the directory of tool.dll.

What works
----------
- D3DCompile / D3DCompile2 / D3DCompileFromFile for vs/ps 1.x-3.0 (D3D9
  bytecode with a CTAB constant table), SM4/SM5 including the
  *_4_0_level_9_x profiles (DXBC), and fx_2_0 / fx_4_x / fx_5_0 effects.
- D3DPreprocess, D3DDisassemble, D3DStripShader, D3DGetBlobPart and the
  signature-blob helpers, D3DCreateBlob, D3DReadFileToBlob,
  D3DWriteBlobToFile.
- D3DReflect with ID3D11ShaderReflection (and ID3D12ShaderReflection) for
  DXBC shaders: constant buffers, variables, types, default values, bound
  resources, signatures.

Not implemented (return E_NOTIMPL): D3DAssemble, D3DCompressShaders,
D3DDecompressShaders, D3DCreateLinker, D3DCreateFunctionLinkingGraph,
D3DLoadModule, D3DReflectLibrary, D3DSetBlobPart, D3DDisassembleRegion,
D3DDisassemble10Effect, D3DDisassemble11Trace,
D3DGetTraceInstructionOffsets. D3DCOMPILE_* optimisation and debug flags
are accepted and ignored; vkd3d always emits its own code.

The output is not byte-identical to Microsoft's compiler (different
instruction selection and register allocation), but register and constant
buffer layout follow the HLSL packing rules, so reflection data match.

Known limitations (vkd3d 2.1 + the patches in this package):
- fx_2_0 effects: parameters and technique/pass structure only; sampler
  state blocks, render-state assignments and "compile vs_2_0 f()" in a
  pass fail with "not yet implemented".
- vkd3d's shader model 2 register allocation is less tight than fxc's:
  long vertex shaders can exceed vs_2_0's 12 temporaries (MonoGame's
  SkinnedEffect needs vs_3_0), and if/return flattening may read
  uninitialised temporaries, which strict validators such as MojoShader
  reject.
- Output is checked against Windows' d3dcompiler_47 on MonoGame's stock
  and test effects: SM4 (*_4_0_level_9_1) constant buffers, variables,
  types, defaults and resource bindings match; SM2 CTAB constants
  (names, register sets, indices, counts, types) match.

Diagnostics: vkd3d prints "fixme:" lines to stderr for ignored flags. Set
VKD3D_SHADER_DEBUG=none and VKD3D_DEBUG=none to silence them.
